### 🛡️ Privacy Policy for AMO Cashier

**Last Updated:** [October 24, 2026]

This Privacy Policy governs the manner in which **AMO Cashier** ("the Service", "the Application") operates. We are committed to protecting your privacy and ensuring the security of your commercial and transaction data[2][4].

---

#### 1\. Information Collection and Use

**A. Business &amp; Store Details** To operate store management and point-of-sale (POS) features, the Application allows merchants to input store details, such as store name, contact phone number, email address, store location, and regional currency[5].

**B. Sales, Inventory &amp; Customer Transaction Data**

* **Customer Information:** When issuing receipts or processing online/delivery orders, you may input customer details (such as customer name, phone number, and delivery address)[4][6].
* **Inventory &amp; Financial Records:** Products, stock quantities, sales invoices, capital, and profit metrics are processed and stored locally on your device or managed through your configured store database[1].

**C. Electronic Tax Compliance Data** If you choose to enable Electronic Invoicing features (e.g., for ZATCA, ETA, FTA, ISTD, NBR, OTA, or MOF-KW), the Application securely stores the merchant tax identification number (VAT Number) and integration credentials (e.g., Client ID, Client Secret, and Private Keys) provided by you[2]. This data is strictly used to sign and generate official electronic invoices and QR codes as required by regional tax regulations[2].

---

#### 2\. Device Permissions Required

To deliver full POS and store management functionality, the Application may request the following permissions:

* **Camera Access:** Used solely to scan product barcodes for quick sales processing and inventory management[3][11].
* **Storage / Local Backup Access:** Used to generate, export, print PDF invoices, and save or restore local store backups[1][7].

---

#### 3\. Log Data and Technical Information

Like most mobile applications, we may access anonymous, non-personal diagnostic data about your device to maintain app stability. This may include:

* Device model and operating system version.
* Aggregated usage statistics and crash logs (collected via standard platform tools like Google Play Console).

This technical data cannot be used to identify you, your customers, or your business personally.

---

#### 4\. Third-Party Services and Tax Integration

The App does not sell or share your business data with third-party advertisers.

When you activate regional **Electronic Tax Compliance**, the Application transmits signed electronic invoices directly to the merchant's designated governmental tax authority (e.g., ZATCA in Saudi Arabia, ETA in Egypt, or FTA in UAE) in accordance with your official merchant integration setup[2][10].

---

#### 5\. Data Security &amp; Storage

All local business databases, calculation records, and offline backups are saved securely on your device[1]. We implement industry-standard encryption and security measures to protect sensitive integration keys and tax details stored within the app[2][9].

---

#### 6\. Children's Privacy

The Service is intended for commercial business use and general audiences, and does not knowingly collect any personally identifiable information from children under the age of 13.

---

#### 7\. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated revision date.

